    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan presents a genuinely balanced risk/reward profile for AMZN. The technical trend structure is bullish \u2014 price sits above all major moving averages in perfect alignment, at 60-day highs with zero drawdown, and the February 2 earnings breakout on 2.6x average volume signals institutional accumulation. However, the stock is extended (26.3% above the 200-day SMA, 10.5% above the 50-day SMA), momentum is decelerating (MACD line down 21% from its February 12 peak, histogram negative for eight sessions), and the stock has been range-bound between $167-$175 for three weeks, repeatedly failing at the $175-$179 resistance zone. Critically, sentiment, news, and macro reports are all blank \u2014 there is no identifiable catalyst to drive the next leg up. With symmetric risk/reward (2.6% upside to $179.47 vs 4.1% downside to $167.82) and no catalyst, adding exposure at these extended levels is not justified, but selling a stock in a confirmed uptrend with exceptional cash generation ($84.9B operating cash flow) is equally unjustified. Hold is the disciplined call.\n\n**Entry Price**: 174.99\n\n**Stop Loss**: 167.82\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position at or below target weight. Do not use leverage. If adding on a pullback to $170-$168, size at half the normal increment.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
